TFLV_Upgrade_RS_HordeMancubus_Name = "Horde: mancubi";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_HordeMancubus_Desc = "kills raise several cheap mancubi at once";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_HordeMancubus_TT = "The other way to spend a kill: instead of one good body, a ring of cheap ones. Levels buy more of them rather than better ones, and they come up spread around the corpse so they do not crowd each other out. Same rules as any minion -- friendly to you, hostile to everything else, and paying XP to the gun that raised them for life. Mastery: five at a time.";

TFLV_Upgrade_RS_BaneMancubus_Name = "Bane: mancubi";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_BaneMancubus_Desc = "you hit mancubi noticeably harder";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_BaneMancubus_TT = "A flat percentage bonus against that family, landing as a separate second hit so it shows on the feed and cannot be eaten by the first hit's resistances. It reads the same bestiary the Levy cards do, so it recognizes every colour variant of the family and not just the base monster. Stacks with everything.";

TFLV_Upgrade_RS_TitheMancubus_Name = "Tithe: mancubi";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_TitheMancubus_Desc = "killing mancubi puts you back together";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_TitheMancubus_TT = "Every mancubi you kill heals you, scaled to how dangerous the bestiary rates that particular one -- so the big members of the family are worth more than the chaff without a hand-written table saying so. It can carry you above your normal maximum. Mastery: they drop ammunition as well.";

TFLV_Upgrade_RS_CullMancubus_Name = "Cull: mancubi";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_CullMancubus_Desc = "wounded mancubi do not get to limp away";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_CullMancubus_TT = "Once a mancubi drops below a share of its own maximum health, your next hit finishes it outright. Because the threshold is a share rather than a flat number, it is worth the same against the biggest member of the family as the smallest. Levels raise the threshold.";

TFLV_Upgrade_RS_LevyCacodemon_Name = "Levy: cacodemons";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_LevyCacodemon_Desc = "kills raise a cacodemons to fight for you";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_LevyCacodemon_TT = "A chance on every kill to raise one good cacodemons on your side, whatever you actually killed. The budget climbs with level and buys further up that family's own roster, so late levels field the dangerous members rather than more of the cheap ones. Yours are friendly to you and hostile to everything else, and every point of damage they deal feeds the gun that raised them for as long as they live -- including after you have switched weapons. Mastery: the budget reaches the top of the family.";

TFLV_Upgrade_RS_HordeCacodemon_Name = "Horde: cacodemons";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_HordeCacodemon_Desc = "kills raise several cheap cacodemons at once";
TFLV_Upgrade_RS_HordeCacodemon_TT = "The other way to spend a kill: instead of one good body, a ring of cheap ones. Levels buy more of them rather than better ones, and they come up spread around the corpse so they do not crowd each other out. Same rules as any minion -- friendly to you, hostile to everything else, and paying XP to the gun that raised them for life. Mastery: five at a time.";

